    "coverage": [
      "Actual compiled queue and playlist consumers with injected geometry at 0/1/80/1000/10000 tracks; bounded mounts and no initial business commands.",
      "Full host-filtered playback order, positions and select-all preserving outside selections; complete queue/playlist batch removal.",
      "Previously offscreen/empty/broad/cleared host results stay bounded; empty restoration finishes without a lazy delegate.",
      "Distant occurrence restore before focus, complete-order keyboard moves in both directions, disposed-adapter rejection and same-scope replacement handoff.",
      "Platform detail uses its complete subset and original positions; growing overview is bounded, moves on the full platform order and returns to a distant entry/offset/focus.",
      "Current queue song remains a host projection, without follow-scroll or replay; switching playlists invalidates pending removal and changes restoration identity.",
      "Throwing lazy loaders prove default/false/foreign consumer gates never execute the virtual candidate."
    ],
    "method": "Node custom Vue renderer with injected boxes and simulated focus/events. Async modules preload only in candidate tests; separate admission tests use throwing loaders. Native layout, actual browser focus, OS capture and frame-time claims are excluded.",
